---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout basePath="" title="The Inner War | Ask Astro Raja">

  <!-- PAGE HEADER -->
  <section class="pt-32 pb-16 px-4 bg-brand-light-bg text-center border-b border-brand-border">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <p class="text-brand-saffron font-bold tracking-[0.2em] uppercase mb-6 text-sm md:text-base">
        The Inner War
      </p>
      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-6xl font-extrabold text-brand-navy mb-6 tracking-tight">Confident outside. Falling apart inside.</h1>
      <p class="text-lg md:text-xl text-brand-text leading-relaxed font-medium max-w-2xl mx-auto">
        "I overthink every decision until the opportunity dies."
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CONTENT -->
  <section class="py-24 px-4 bg-white">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto space-y-16">
      
      <div class="prose prose-lg prose-brand max-w-none text-brand-navy">
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-6">The Exhaustion of the Mask</h2>
        <p class="mb-6">
          You look like you have it all together. People come to you for advice. You project competence and control. But inside, your mind is a war zone. You overthink every minor detail, second-guess your intuition, and say yes to everyone until you have absolutely nothing left for yourself.
        </p>

        <div class="bg-slate-50 border-l-4 border-brand-saffron p-8 my-10 rounded-r-2xl">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-brand-navy mb-4">The Invisible Symptom</h3>
          <p class="mb-0">
            This isn't imposter syndrome; it's a structural misalignment in your behavioral blueprint. Your "safe baseline" requires you to over-deliver and over-analyze to prevent criticism. You are reacting to life's demands instead of designing your own path because your system believes that maintaining the mask is the only way to survive.
          </p>
        </div>

        <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">The Pattern</h3>
        <p class="mb-6">
          The cycle looks like this: Opportunity arises -> Instant internal pressure to execute perfectly -> Paralysis by analysis -> The opportunity passes -> Deep frustration at your own inaction -> Vow to "do better next time" -> Another opportunity arises.
        </p>

        <p class="mb-10">
          You know your potential, but this hidden code keeps holding you back. You have to locate the exact trigger in your blueprint and disable it.
        </p>

        <div class="text-center mt-16 pt-12 border-t border-brand-border">
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-brand-navy mb-6">Diagnose Your Operating System</h3>
          <p class="text-brand-text mb-8 max-w-xl mx-auto">
            Stop fighting the inner war with positive affirmations. Understand the behavioral blueprint that is causing the friction, and get the exact daily system to rewrite it.
          </p>
          <a href="/get-reading" class="inline-block px-8 py-4 bg-brand-navy text-white rounded-xl font-bold text-lg hover:scale-105 hover:bg-brand-purple transition-transform shadow-lg hover:shadow-xl">
            Discover My Pattern
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

</Layout>
